## My answer to the user prompt

Do you mean **automatic cleanup of an ordinary linked list**, or a **tracing garbage collector that also handles cycles**? For an ordinary singly linked list, C++ smart pointers provide automatic cleanup without writing a garbage collector.

Here is a C++14 example. It frees nodes iteratively, avoiding recursive destruction that could overflow the stack for a very long list.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <memory>
#include <utility>

class LinkedList {
    struct Node {
        int value;
        std::unique_ptr<Node> next;

        explicit Node(int v) : value(v) {}
    };

    std::unique_ptr<Node> head;

public:
    LinkedList() = default;

    // This example gives each list exclusive ownership of its nodes.
    LinkedList(const LinkedList&) = delete;
    LinkedList& operator=(const LinkedList&) = delete;

    ~LinkedList() {
        clear();
    }

    void push_front(int value) {
        auto node = std::make_unique<Node>(value);
        node->next = std::move(head);
        head = std::move(node);
    }

    void pop_front() noexcept {
        if (head) {
            auto old = std::move(head);
            head = std::move(old->next);
            // old now owns only the removed node, which is freed here.
        }
    }

    void clear() noexcept {
        while (head) {
            pop_front();
        }
    }

    void print() const {
        for (const Node* p = head.get(); p; p = p->next.get()) {
            std::cout << p->value << " -> ";
        }
        std::cout << "nullptr\n";
    }
};

int main() {
    LinkedList list;
    list.push_front(10);
    list.push_front(20);
    list.push_front(30);
    list.print();  // 30 -> 20 -> 10 -> nullptr
} // All nodes are automatically freed.
```

This is **RAII-based ownership**, not tracing garbage collection: nodes are reclaimed when removed or when the list is destroyed. For a standard-library solution, `std::forward_list<int>` already manages its nodes automatically. Cyclic or shared-node structures need a different ownership design.

