## Correct solution

The original order matters: we cannot necessarily keep the largest elements.

### 1. Characterize the remaining elements

The final length is
\[
r=(n-1)\bmod k+1.
\]
Let \(q=(n-r)/k\), the number of operations.

Suppose the surviving original positions are \(p_1<p_2<\cdots<p_r\). Every gap before, between, or after survivors must contain a multiple of \(k\) deleted elements: no operation can cross an element that survives.

Therefore, precisely the valid survivor sequences have
\[
p_j=j+t_jk,\qquad 0\le t_1\le t_2\le\cdots\le t_r\le q.
\]
Conversely, every such sequence is achievable by deleting each gap in blocks of \(k\).

### 2. Check a candidate median

For a candidate \(X\), call an element good if it is at least \(X\). Because the problem uses the lower median, we need at least
\[
\text{need}=\left\lfloor\frac r2\right\rfloor+1
\]
good survivors.

We maximize their number with dynamic programming.

Process \(t=0,\ldots,q\), and within each row process \(j=1,\ldots,r\). Maintain `dp[j]`, the maximum number of good elements among the first \(j\) survivors using processed rows.

The transition is
\[
dp[j]=\max\bigl(dp[j],\,dp[j-1]+[a_{tk+j}\ge X]\bigr).
\]

- Keeping the old value skips row \(t\) for survivor \(j\).
- The second option chooses position \(tk+j\).
- Updating \(j\) in increasing order permits consecutive survivors to use the same row, enforcing nondecreasing row numbers.

There are \((q+1)r\le n\) transitions, so each check is \(O(n)\). Binary search finds the largest feasible \(X\).

### C++17

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int t;
    cin >> t;

    while (t--) {
        int n, k;
        cin >> n >> k;

        vector<int> a(n);
        int mx = 0;
        for (int &x : a) {
            cin >> x;
            mx = max(mx, x);
        }

        int r = (n - 1) % k + 1;
        int q = (n - r) / k;
        int need = r / 2 + 1;

        vector<int> dp(r + 1);
        const int NEG = -1000000000;

        auto feasible = [&](int x) {
            fill(dp.begin(), dp.end(), NEG);
            dp[0] = 0;

            for (int row = 0; row <= q; ++row) {
                for (int j = 1; j <= r; ++j) {
                    int good = (a[row * k + j - 1] >= x);
                    dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[j - 1] + good);
                }
            }

            return dp[r] >= need;
        };

        int lo = 1, hi = mx;
        while (lo < hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo + 1) / 2;
            if (feasible(mid))
                lo = mid;
            else
                hi = mid - 1;
        }

        cout << lo << '\n';
    }
}
```

**Complexity:** \(O(n\log \max a_i)\) time per test case and \(O(n)\) total space, including the input array.

